$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides:
5-(sec-Butyl)furan-2-carbaldehyde (Table 2, Row 4, Column 2, Entry 2).
The general procedure was employed with the following modifications: 5
mol% NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, 22 h reaction time. A brown oil (118
mg, 71%) was isolated by column chromatography (gradient from 75:25 to
70:30 Hex:EtOAc). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 9.50 (s, 1H), 7.15 (d, J =
3.5 Hz, 1H), 6.20 (d, J = 3.5 Hz, 1H), 2.81 (app. sextet, J = 6.9 Hz,
1H), 1.66 (m, 2H), 1.26 (d, J = 7.1 Hz, 2H), 0.87 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H)
ppm. 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 177.1, 168.2, 151.8, 123.5, 107.6, 35.3,
28.4, 18.3, 11.5 ppm.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (70:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Nickel-Catalyzed Negishi Cross-Coupling Reactions of Secondary Alkylzinc
Halides and Aryl Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Joshi-Pangu, Amruta; Ganesh, Madhu; Biscoe, Mark R.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2011), 13(5), 1218-1221

