$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for cross-coupling reactions
of zinc reagents 1f and aryl bromide (TP5) To a solution of aryl bromide
(0.5 mmol) in THF (0.5 mL) were added S-Phos (12 mg, 6 mol%), Pd(OAc)2
(3.4 mg, 3 mol%). Then, a solution of benzyl zinc chloride 1f (0.75 mmol,
1.5 eq.) in THF-DMSO was added dropwise (Eq. (3)). The reaction mixture
was stirred for 10-24 h at 25 °C, then quenched by adding sat. aqueous
NH4Cl. The layers were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with
diethyl ether (5 × 50 mL). The combined organic extracts were dried over
Na2SO4. Evaporation of the solvents in vacuo and purification by flash
chromatography (silica gel, isohexane/EA = 10:1). The title coupling
products (3a'-3g). Ethyl
4-(2-(2-(tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2-methylpropanamido)-1-phenylpropyl)benzoate
(3a', according to TP5).
2-(Tert-butyldimethylsilyloxy)-2-methyl-N-(1-(3-(trifluoromethyl)
phenyl)-1-phenylpropan-2-yl)propanamide (3d, according to TP5). A
yellowish oil, d.r. > 95:5 (anti/syn). Anti-isomer: 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.58-7.50 (m, 2H), 7.29-7.17 (m, 6H), 6.73 (br, 1H), 4.83-4.71
(m, 1H), 3.87 (d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1H), 1.35 (s, 3H), 1.35 (s, 3H), 1.13 (d, J
= 6.8 Hz, 3H), 0.91 (s, 3H), 0.77 (s, 9H), 0.05(s, 3H), -0.06 (s, 3H).
13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 175.7, 163.2 (d, J = 260.6 Hz), 151.0 (d, J =
9.7 Hz), 139.7, 133.6, 128.9, 128.2, 127.4, 124.6 (d, J = 3.1 Hz), 116.2
(d, J = 20.1 Hz), 113.8, 76.6, 58.7, 46.4, 29.7, 27.6, 27.4, 25.7, 20.5,
17.9, -2.4. IR (KBr, cm-1) ν 3381, 2237, 1651, 1569, 1202, 874, 723. MS
(EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 439 [M+-Me] (4), 397 (34), 341 (8), 311 (9), 281
(8), 244(21), 207 (31), 173 (100), 115 (21), 73 (49). HRMS (EI): calcd
for C26H36F3NO2Si: 454.2452, found: 454.2448.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, Negishi coupling, >95:5 anti:syn
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective C(sp3)-C(sp2) Negishi coupling of
(2-amido-1-phenylpropyl)zinc compounds through the steric control of
β-amido group
