$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the cross-coupling of
aryl iodides and secondary alkylzinc iodides: 5-(sec-Butyl)-1H-indole
(Table 2, Row 4, Column 1, Entry 2). The general procedure was employed
with the following modifications: 2.5 equiv. alkylzinc reagent employed,
5 mol% NiCl2 and terpyridine employed, 48 h reaction time. A yellow
liquid (130mg, 75 %) was isolated by column chromatography (gradient from
75:25 to 70:30 Hex:EtOAc). 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 8.04 (bs, 1H), 7.47
(s, 1H), 7.33 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.18 (m, 1H), 7.08 (dd, J = 8.8 Hz,
1.5 Hz, 1H), 6.52 (m, 1H), 2.71 (m, 1H), 1.67 (m, 2H), 1.32 (d, J = 6.8
Hz, 3H), 0.87 (t, J = 7.3 Hz, 3H) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ: 139.3,
134.5, 128.0, 124.3, 121.8, 118.6, 110.8, 102.4, 41.9, 31.8, 22.7, 12.6
ppm. IR (neat, cm-1): 3415, 2960, 2927, 2872, 1475, 1455, 1414, 1354,
1092, 894, 805, 726. Anal. Calcd. for C12H15N: C, 83.19; H, 8.73. Found:
C, 82.76; H, 8.87.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective (>100:1 s-Bu product:n-Bu product), Negishi cross-coupling
reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
