$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In the case of aminocarbene complexes, a
solution of aminocarbene 1e or 4a (1.0 equiv) and PdCl2XantPhos (5 mol %)
was added to the solution of organozinc reagent (1.2 equiv). The
resultant mixture was stirred for 3 h at ambient temperature and quenched
with brine, and the water layer was extracted with ether (3 x 30 mL).
Combined organic layers were dried (MgSO4) and concentrated in vacuo, and
column chromatography (silica gel) afforded the product. Alternatively,
the title compound was prepared following the general procedure B
starting from 4a (0.335 g, 0.83 mmol), iPrMgCl·LiCl (0.85 mL, 1.05 mmol),
ZnBr2 (0.225 g, 1.0 mmol), ethyl 4-iodobenzoate (0.276 g, 1.0 mmol) and
PdCl2XantPhos (0.031 g, 0.042 mmol) giving 0.290 g of the 5c (74%).
Pentacarbonyl[(N,N-dimethylamino)(4'-ethoxycarbonyl-4-biphenyl)methylene]chromium(0).
Mp: >117 °C dec. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 1.42 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 3H, CH3), 3.12
(s, 3H, CH3), 4.03 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.41 (q, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H, CH2), 6.81 (d J
= 8.1 Hz, 2H, CH), 7.65−7.69 (m, 4H, CH), 8.11 (d J = 8.1 Hz, 2H, CH).
13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 14.3, 46.0, 51.3, 60.9, 119.6, 126.6, 127.4, 129.3,
130.0, 137.2, 144.4, 152.1, 166.4, 217.1, 223.7, 274.4. IR (ATR): ν 2052
(m), 1970 (w), 1937 (m), 1878 (s), 1710 (m), 1608 (m), 1541 (m), 1402
(w), 1365 (w), 1274 (m), 1103 (m), cm-1. Anal. Calcd for C23H19CrNO7: C,
58.35; H, 4.05; N, 2.96. Found: C, 58.64; H, 4.23; N, 2.83
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
