$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Negishi Cross-Coupling Reaction; General
Procedure 2 Halide (10 mmol), Pd2dba3·CHCl3 (263 mg, 0.25 mmol, 2.5
mol%), dppf (282 mg, 0.5 mmol, 5 mol%), THF (75 mL) and the organozinc
reagent solution 1 (14 mmol, 1.4 equiv) were stirred for 24-48 h at 50 °C
under argon atmosphere. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to 25
°C, quenched with sat. NH4Cl (20 mL) and extracted several times with
EtOAc. The combined organic phases were washed with H2O (10 mL) and brine
(10 mL) and dried (Na2SO4). After removal of all volatiles, the residue
was purified by column chromatography (Table 2). Ethyl
3-(2-Methoxynaphthalen-1-yl)propiolate (2) Prepared from
1-iodo-2-methoxynaphthalene (5.67 g, 19.6 mmol) and 1 (94 mL, 23.5 mmol),
following General Procedure 2; The spectroscopic data are in accordance
with the published data.16 Ethyl 3-(2-Methoxyphenyl)propiolate (30)25
Prepared by Pd-catalyzed cross-coupling reaction of
1-iodo-2-methoxybenzene (17; 6.2 mL, 45 mmol) with 1 (252 mL, 63 mmol),
following General Procedure 2. The expected ester 30 was obtained after
chromatography. 72% yield (6.59 g). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.44
(dd, J = 7.5, 1.7 Hz, 1 H), 7.33 (ddd, J = 8.7, 7.0, 1.8 Hz, 1 H), 6.86
(dd, J = 7.5, 1.0 Hz, 1 H), 6.83 (d, J = 8.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.22 (q, J = 7.1
Hz, 2 H), 3.81 (s, 3 H), 1.27 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 170.2, 161.5, 134.8, 132.3, 120.5, 110.7, 108.7, 84.6, 83.1,
61.9, 55.7, 14.0. MS (EI, 70 eV): m/z (%) = 204 (30, [M+]), 159 (25), 132
(100), 115 (17), 103 (12), 88 (14), 77 (23). HRMS (EI): m/z calcd for
C12H12O3 (M+): 204.0781; found: 204.0782.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Negishi cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM On the synthesis of arylpropiolic acids and investigations towards the
formation of vinyl chlorides by HCl addition during esterification
reactions
