$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The in situ generated diarylzinc reagent was
dissolved in DMF (5 mL). CuI (9.5 mg, 0.050 mmol), aryl halide (1.0
mmol), and LiCl (42.3 mg, 1.0 mmol) were weighed into a 15-mL pressure
vessel and the diarylzinc reagent was added. The pressure vessel was then
tightly capped, taken out of the glovebox, and placed in an oil bath
preheated to 100 °C with vigorous stirring. After 12 h, the mixture was
cooled to r.t., diluted with EtOAc (15 mL) and washed with H2O (3 × 5
mL); the aqueous fraction was back-extracted with EtOAc (3 × 5 mL). All
of the EtOAc extracts were combined and dried (Na2SO4), and the solvent
was removed on a rotary evaporator. The product was purified by column
chromatography (silica gel, 0–10% EtOAc–hexanes). 4-Methylbiphenyl (3)
4-Methoxybiphenyl (4) Purification by column chromatography (silica gel)
gave 4 as a white solid; yield: 132.6 mg (72%). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3):
δ = 3.91 (s, 3 H), 7.08 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 2 H), 7.41 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1 H),
7.51 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 2 H), 7.61–7.68 (m, 4 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 55.3, 114.3, 126.7, 126.8, 128.2, 128.8, 133.8, 140.8, 159.2. GC-MS:
m/z = 184.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM glove box used, Negishi coupling, sealed pressure vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Copper-catalyzed Negishi coupling of diarylzinc reagents with aryl
iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Thapa, Surendra; Vangala, Adarsh S.; Giri, Ramesh
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2016), 48(4), 504-511

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME290 STEP1
$RXN



