$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl
(5-(tert-butyldimethylsilanyloxymethyl)-4-methoxy-2-methoxymethoxyphenyl)-acetate
(5). Zinc bromide (1.56 g, 6.92 mmol) in a dry flask was heated at 140 °C
for 1 h under high vacuum. Then a mixture of
(5-bromo-2-methoxy-4-methoxymethoxy-benzyloxy)-tert-butyldimethylsilane
(6) (1.93 g, 4.94 mmol), α-(tributylstannyl)acetate (2.61 g, 6.92 mmol),
and PdCl2 (o-tol3P)2 (310 mg, 0.395 mmol) in dry DMF (10 mL) was added to
the flask and heated at 80 °C for 14 h under argon. The black reaction
mixture was diluted with water (10 mL) and extracted with Et2O (3 × 10
mL). The combined organic layers were washed with brine, dried over
anhydrous MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated under reduced pressure. The
crude resi- due was further purified by flash chromatography on silica
gel (15:1, hexanes-EtOAc). (1.41 g, 3.58 mmol, 72%) as a pale yellow oil.
Rf= 0.43 (3:1 v/v hexanes-EtOAc). 1H-NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ 7.23 (s, 1H,
H6), 6.67 (s, 1H, H3), 5.16 (s, 2H, ArOCH2OCH3), 4.68 (d, 2H, J= 3.9 Hz,
ArCH2OTBS), 4.14 (q, 2H, J= 7.2 Hz, OCH2CH3), 3.79 (s, 1H, ArOMe), 3.58
(s, 2H, ArCH2COOEt), 3.49 (s, 3H, ArOCH2OCH3), 1.24 (t, 3H, J= 7.2 Hz,
OCH2CH3), 0.94[(s, 9H, SiC(CH3)3]. 13C-NMR (CDCl3, 75 MHz): δ 172.1,
156.1, 155.0, 129.3, 122.9, 115.2, 97.9, 94.8, 60.5, 59.9, 55.9, 55.3,
35.6, 25.9, 18.4, 14.2, -5.3. IR (KBr, neat): 2955, 2931, 2903, 2855,
1737, 1618, 1509, 1465, 1254, 1215, 1191, 1153, 1116, 1091, 1073, 1021,
996, 838, 776 cm-1. LRMS (ESI): m/z 421[M+Na]+. HRMS (ESI): calcd for
C20H34O6SiNa [M+Na]+ : 421.2101, found: 421.2101.
